I left out the `aap:caps/http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The graph definition declares only `StateHandle<'subscriptions', read>` for this node, and the approval you describe isn't in the spec I was given. Adding a network import would also send a request to an external host that the graph doesn't authorize. `RunInfo` has no text field, so the "input's text" the enrichment URL would use doesn't exist. Once the graph definition includes the http-client grant, the enrichment fetch can be added as a separate change with a defined source for the query.

